{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:18789896 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:18789896 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"18789896","source":"MED","pmid":"18789896","doi":"10.1016/j.bbrc.2008.09.006","title":"trans-Dienelactone hydrolase from Pseudomonas reinekei MT1, a novel zinc-dependent hydrolase.","authorString":"Cámara B, Marín M, Schlömann M, Hecht HJ, Junca H, Pieper DH.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Cámara B","lastName":"Cámara","firstName":"Beatriz","initials":"B","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5227-7499"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Microbial Pathogenesis, HZI-Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research, Inhoffenstr. 7, 38124 Braunschweig, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Marín M","lastName":"Marín","firstName":"Macarena","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6966-2446"}},{"fullName":"Schlömann M","lastName":"Schlömann","firstName":"Michael","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Hecht HJ","lastName":"Hecht","firstName":"Hans-Jürgen","initials":"HJ"},{"fullName":"Junca H","lastName":"Junca","firstName":"Howard","initials":"H","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4546-6229"}},{"fullName":"Pieper DH","lastName":"Pieper","firstName":"Dietmar H","initials":"DH"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5227-7499"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6966-2446"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4546-6229"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"2","volume":"376","journalIssueId":1569285,"dateOfPublication":"2008 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":2008,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Biochem Biophys Res Commun","title":"Biochemical and biophysical research communications","essn":"1090-2104","issn":"0006-291X","isoabbreviation":"Biochem Biophys Res Commun","nlmid":"0372516"},"printPublicationDate":"2008-11-01"},"pubYear":"2008","pageInfo":"423-428","abstractText":"Pseudomonas reinekei MT1 is capable of growing on 4- and 5-chlorosalicylate, involving a pathway with trans-dienelactone hydrolase (trans-DLH) as a key enzyme. It acts on 4-chloromuconolactone formed during cycloisomerization of 3-chloromuconate by hydrolyzing it to maleylacetate. The gene encoding this activity was localized, sequenced and expressed in Escherichia coli. Inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry showed that both the wild-type as well as recombinant enzymes contained 2 moles of zinc but variable amounts of manganese/mol of protein subunit. The inactive metal-free apoenzyme could be reactivated by Zn(2+) or Mn(2+). Thus, trans-DLH is a Zn(2+)-dependent hydrolase using halosubstituted muconolactones and trans-dienelactone as substrates, where Mn(2+) can substitute for Zn(2+). It is the first member of COG1878 and PF04199 for which a direct physiological function has been reported.","affiliation":"Department of Microbial Pathogenesis, HZI-Helmholtz Centre for Infection Research, Inhoffenstr. 7, 38124 Braunschweig, Germany.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pseudomonas","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Escherichia coli","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Manganese","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Zinc","meshQualifierList":